## 7. Bottom-line recommendation

Refinance — every option beats staying at 10.8% variable, and fixed protects you from the climb toward 12%. Pay off the $2,068 loan in cash first if your emergency fund survives it. Choose the shortest term whose *required* payment you can guarantee in your worst month — for most drilling Guard members with student schedules that's the **7-year 5.21% ($557.22)** or **10-year 5.51% ($425.11)** plan — then pay more than the minimum every month you can, since there's no prepayment penalty and the extra goes straight at principal. Enroll in autopay for the 0.25% discount. If you're activated on qualifying orders before signing, invoke SCRA on the old loans first and refinance after. Use the Oklahoma tuition waiver, Federal TA, and MGIB-SR so you never borrow for school again.

